# .iwikiignore — drop pages from the iwiki index, gitignore-style.
# Rename to `.iwikiignore` (drop `.example`) to activate. Read relative to the
# engine's working directory (the project root it runs in). By default, with no
# .iwikiignore file, the whole project's wiki pages are indexed.
#
# Real gitignore semantics (via pathspec): patterns match each generated wiki
# page's path (e.g. `docs/wiki/command.md`). A bare name matches at any depth;
# a leading `/` anchors to the root; a trailing `/` matches a directory subtree;
# `!` re-includes; `**` and `#` comments work as in .gitignore.

# Example: drop command/launcher reference pages from semantic search.
command.md
launcher.md

# Anchor to a specific path instead of matching the basename anywhere:
/docs/wiki/html-report.md

# Drop an archive subtree but keep one page:
docs/wiki/archive/
!docs/wiki/archive/keep.md
